ine hydroxylase (PAH) is an essential enzyme that plays a critical role in the metabolism of phenylalanine, converting it into tyrosine. A deficiency in PAH is the underlying cause of phenylketonuria (PKU), a genetic disorder that can lead to serious health issues if not managed properly. In the context of treatment, the functional gene for PAH is introduced in gene therapy to address this deficiency in patients with PKU.", "BH4:Tetrahydrobiopterin is a cofactor necessary for the activity of phenylalanine hydroxylase and is involved in the metabolism of phenylalanine.", "DHPR:Dihydropteridine reductase is an enzyme that plays a role in the regeneration of tetrahydrobiopterin, which is crucial for neurotransmitter synthesis.", "PKU:Phenylketonuria (PKU) is a genetic and metabolic disorder characterized by the accumulation of phenylalanine in the body. If left untreated, this accumulation can lead to severe neurological issues. To prevent such damage, individuals with PKU require careful dietary management to control their phenylalanine levels.", "HPA:Hyperphenylalaninemia benign (HPA) is a mild form of phenylketonuria characterized by lower levels of phenylalanine that do not require dietary treatment.", "IVS10:IVS10 is the most common mutation associated with phenylketonuria in Southern Europe, affecting the PAH gene.", "CROMOSOMA 12:Chromosome 12 is where the PAH gene is located, which is responsible for phenylketonuria.", "DIAGNOSTICO BIOQUIMICO:Biochemical diagnosis of phenylketonuria is established through the measurement of plasma phenylalanine levels.", "CASEN RECORDATI:Casen Recordati is a commercial entity that produces special formulas for low-Phe diets in Spain.", "MEAD-JHONSON:Mead-Jhonson is a company that offers various products for managing phenylketonuria (PKU) diets.", "MILUPA SA:Milupa SA is a manufacturer of specialized dietary products for patients with phenylketonuria.", "NUTRICIA SA:Nutricia SA provides nutritional products tailored for individuals with dietary restrictions, including those with PKU.", "SCIENTIFIC HOSPITAL SUPPLIES (SHS):Scientific Hospital Supplies (SHS) offers a range of dietary products for managing phenylketonuria."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}